      "physical_description": "Kalaga (wall hanging) made of black woollen cloth with applique work in cotton damask, satin, calico and velvet. Embroidered in silver sequins, silver and silver gilt thread spirals and beads imitating pearls.\n\nThe subject represents a Princess of the Konbaung Dynasty (1752-1885) and in the costume of the 19th century. She stands full-front, against a black background, with earrings, necklace, bracelets of imitation pearls and a floral headdress, the right arm bent, the left pendant. The ein-gyi (outer jacket) is yellow, the yinzi (breast cloth) red, the hta-mein (wrap-round skirt) to which is attached a white train, is magenta with acheik patterns. All the garments are heavily sequined in a variety of motifs. The earrings are of looking glass. The flower in the headdress is of pink Berlin wool.",
